      atm: 'ATMs are everywhere in major cities. Most foreign bank cards work at Bank of China, ICBC, and CCB ATMs with UnionPay, Plus, or Cirrus logos. Withdrawal fees vary — typically ¥10–30 per transaction for foreign cards. WeChat Pay and Alipay now support foreign bank cards for in-store and online payments.',
      usd: 'Chinese Yuan (CNY/RMB) is the only currency for daily transactions. USD is not widely accepted but can be exchanged at banks, hotels, and exchange booths. China has capital controls — moving large amounts of money in and out of China can be restricted. Expat employees can remit a portion of their salary abroad with proper tax documentation. Wise and Revolut have limited functionality in China.',
