      public: 'Hangzhou has good public hospitals, especially those affiliated with Zhejiang University. Top facilities: First Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University School of Medicine (one of the best in eastern China), Sir Run Run Shaw Hospital, Zhejiang Provincial People\'s Hospital, and Hangzhou First People\'s Hospital. Standards are high in specialized departments but wait times can be long and Mandarin is needed.',
      private: 'International healthcare options are more limited than in Shanghai or Beijing. Facilities include: Zhejiang University International Hospital, Sir Run Run Shaw Hospital (some international services), and several private medical and dental clinics. Many expats go to Shanghai for specialized international care or use medical travel services. International insurance is accepted at some private clinics.',
      insurance: 'International health insurance ranges from ¥6,000–18,000+/year. Many tech employers provide health insurance. Out-of-pocket GP visits at private clinics cost ¥300–800. Public hospital visits are very affordable (¥30–200). Some expats prefer to go to Shanghai for international-standard healthcare, as it\'s only a 45-minute high-speed train ride away.',
