      note: 'Hangzhou has a humid subtropical climate similar to Shanghai but slightly milder. The plum rain season can be gray and dreary. Air quality is generally better than Beijing and slightly better than Shanghai, thanks to the lake and surrounding green hills. The nearby tea hills and mountains offer easy access to nature and hiking — a big quality-of-life bonus for expats who love the outdoors.',
