            desc: 'The Altstadt (Old Town) is the historic and geographic center of Munich. This is where you find Marienplatz with its famous Glockenspiel, the towering Frauenkirche (Cathedral of Our Lady), the elaborate Rathaus (New Town Hall), and the historic Viktualienmarkt food market. The Altstadt is a mix of medieval streets, grand 19th-century boulevards (Max-Joseph-Platz, Odeonsplatz), and bustling shopping streets (Kaufingerstraße, Neuhauser Straße). It is also the center of Munich beer culture — the famous Hofbräuhaus is here, along with countless beer gardens and traditional Bavarian restaurants. During Oktoberfest, the whole city (and the world) comes to Munich, and the Altstadt buzzes with festival energy. Despite being a major tourist destination, the Altstadt has a permanent population and a strong Bavarian identity.',
