            desc: 'The Altstadt is home to a mix of long-time Munich residents, professionals, expats, shopkeepers, and people working in tourism and hospitality. It is an expensive and desirable place to live. Many expats who work in the city center choose to live here for the convenience and the classic Munich experience. The neighborhood attracts professionals, couples, and people who love being in the middle of everything. Families often prefer Schwabing, Bogenhausen, or other neighborhoods with more parks and space. The Altstadt has a large international presence due to the many multinational companies, hotels, and cultural institutions located in and near the center. During Oktoberfest and other major events, the population swells with tourists.',
