            title: 'Getting Around',
            desc: 'The city center is walkable but hilly — Stuttgart is in a valley basin, so going to surrounding neighborhoods involves climbing hills. The public transit system (VVS — Stuttgart Transport Association) includes U-Bahn, S-Bahn, Stadtbahn (light rail), and buses — all integrated. The U-Bahn and Stadtbahn connect the center to most neighborhoods. The S-Bahn connects to suburbs and the airport. Stuttgart Airport (STR) is about 20 minutes by S-Bahn (S3 line). Stuttgart Hauptbahnhof (main station) is a major rail hub — currently undergoing a massive reconstruction (Stuttgart 21 project). High-speed ICE trains go to Munich (2.5h), Frankfurt (1.5h), and other cities. Stuttgart is a very car-oriented city — it is the home of Mercedes and Porsche, after all. Many families have cars. The Autobahn network is excellent — you can be in the Black Forest in an hour. Parking in the center is expensive but most apartment buildings have underground parking.',
