      note: 'Copenhagen is a very safe city. Denmark consistently ranks as one of the safest and happiest countries in the world. Violent crime is extremely rare. Petty theft (pickpocketing, bike theft) exists but is not a major problem. The main safety concerns are related to biking (car doors, right turns) rather than crime. Expats feel very safe in Copenhagen. The city is clean, well-organized, and people are trustworthy. You can leave your laptop unattended in a cafe and it will likely still be there.',
