      cost: 'Very affordable for residents. GP visits: free. Hospital stays: free. Dental care: not fully covered (you pay some out-of-pocket). Prescription drugs: subsidized. Overall very low out-of-pocket costs.',
      emergency: '112 for emergencies (same number for police, fire, and medical). Excellent emergency services. Fast ambulance response times. Rigshospitalet has a top-level ER.',
      note: 'Denmark has one of the best healthcare systems in the world. High quality, universal access, and essentially free at the point of use. The system is funded through high taxes. Wait times can be long for non-urgent elective procedures — this is the main complaint. For urgent and emergency care, it is excellent. Most doctors speak excellent English. The Danish healthcare system is consistently ranked among the best in the world by the WHO and other organizations. Dental care is only partially covered and can be expensive.',
