      retirement: {
        duration: 'SRRV (Special Resident Retiree Visa) — lifetime',
        income: 'Deposit of $10,000–$50,000 depending on age and type',
        desc: 'The SRRV is a very popular retirement visa. Available to foreigners 35 years and older (yes, very young!) who make a bank deposit (amount depends on age and type). The deposit can be used for investment in certain cases. Grants permanent resident status. Can work, study, or do business in the Philippines. One of the easiest and most affordable retirement/residency programs in the world.',
      },
      note: 'The Philippines has very accessible visa options. Tourist visas are easy to get and can be extended for up to 3 years — very unusual and popular with digital nomads and long-term travelers. The SRRV (Special Resident Retiree Visa) is one of the easiest and most affordable residency programs in the world — available from age 35 with a $10,000–$50,000 bank deposit. The 9(g) work visa is available for employees. The Philippines does not offer an easy path to citizenship — naturalization is difficult and rare. However, permanent residency is relatively easy through SRRV or other programs. The immigration system can be bureaucratic and slow — many people use a visa agent. Overall, the Philippines has one of the most accessible visa regimes in Southeast Asia for long-term stays.',
