      scams: null,
      note: 'Jakarta is generally safe for expats and tourists, especially in upscale and expat neighborhoods (SCBD, Menteng, Kemang, Pondok Indah). However, like any megacity, you need to exercise normal precautions. Petty theft (pickpocketing, bag/phone snatching) is common in crowded areas — keep your belongings secure and be aware of your surroundings. Snatch theft by motorbike riders is a known issue — never hold your phone while walking or in a vehicle with the window down. Terrorism has been a concern in Indonesia (with past bombings in Bali and Jakarta), but security has improved significantly in recent years and major incidents are rare. Always use Gojek or Grab instead of hailing taxis on the street to avoid scams. Traffic safety is also a major concern — Jakarta has terrible traffic and many accidents. Overall, most expats feel safe in the good neighborhoods and take normal precautions.',
