      nightSafety: null,
      scams: null,
      note: 'Bali is generally a very safe destination — one of the safest in Indonesia for tourists. Violent crime against foreigners is rare. However, petty theft (pickpocketing, bag snatching, theft from scooters) does happen — keep your belongings secure and be aware of your surroundings. Money changer scams are well-known — always use reputable money changers and count your money carefully. The biggest safety concern by far is traffic — scooter accidents are common and can be serious. Always wear a helmet, drive defensively, and do not ride after drinking. Many expats and tourists get into scooter accidents. Natural hazards include occasional earthquakes (Indonesia is on the Ring of Fire) and volcanic activity (Mount Agung and Mount Batur are active). Overall, most people feel very safe in Bali and the main safety concern is traffic.',
