      traffic: 'Moderate — traffic is not terrible compared to other major cities because so many people bike and use public transit. Parking is very expensive and limited, discouraging car use.',
      best: 'Biking (faster than cars for most trips). Public transit (tram/metro/bus). Living in the same part of the city as work. Many people work from home part-time.',
      note: 'Commuting in Amsterdam is easy compared to most major cities because of the excellent bike and public transit infrastructure. Most commuters bike — it is faster than driving for trips under 5 km and it is the norm. The bike lane network is extensive and safe. Public transit (trams, metro, buses) is also excellent — clean, frequent, and reliable. Many people also work from home part-time (the Netherlands has one of the highest rates of part-time work and flexible schedules in Europe). The city is compact — you can bike from one side of the center to the other in about 20 minutes. Schiphol Airport is 20 minutes by train from the city center — very convenient for international travel. Parking in the city is very expensive and hard to find, which discourages car use. Overall, commuting in Amsterdam is a breeze compared to most major cities.',
