      overview: 'Modern, advanced banking system. Major Dutch banks (ING, ABN AMRO, Rabobank) dominate. Good English service. Excellent digital and mobile banking. Bunq is a popular Dutch neobank with expats. iDEAL is the dominant payment method.',
      req: 'Passport/residence permit, BSN (burgerservicenummer — personal ID number), proof of address. Relatively easy to open an account as an expat. Can be done online at some banks. BSN required for full access.',
      fees: 'Low fees. Basic current accounts €2–6/month. ATM withdrawals free at your banks ATMs. International transfer fees vary. Overall low fees.',
      atms: 'ATMs everywhere. Most accept international cards (Visa/Mastercard). Free withdrawals from your own bank. Withdrawal fees at other banks ATMs.',
      cards: 'Cards (debit) universally accepted. The Netherlands is largely cashless — cards (pin) and iDEAL are used for almost everything. Mobile payments (Apple Pay, Google Pay) are very common. Cash is declining but still accepted at most places.',
      online: 'Excellent online and mobile banking. Dutch banks have very good apps. You can do almost everything online. iDEAL is the instant bank transfer payment system used everywhere. Instant transfers between banks (SEPA Instant) are available.',
      note: 'The Netherlands has one of the most advanced and digitized banking systems in the world. ING, ABN AMRO, and Rabobank are the big three Dutch banks — all have excellent digital services and English support for expats. Bunq is a popular Dutch neobank that is very expat-friendly. Opening a bank account is relatively straightforward for expats — you need a residence permit and a BSN (social security/ID number). Many banks let you start the process online. iDEAL is the dominant payment system in the Netherlands — most online payments use it. The country is very cashless — most people use debit cards or mobile payments. Cash is still accepted but declining. Revolut and Wise are also very popular with expats for international transfers and travel. Overall, banking in the Netherlands is easy, modern, and efficient — one of the best systems in Europe.',
