      nightSafety: null,
      scams: null,
      note: 'Zagreb is generally a very safe city — one of the safer capitals in Europe. Violent crime is rare and the city has a low crime rate overall. Petty theft (pickpocketing, bike theft) happens occasionally, especially in tourist areas, on public transport, and at the central station — but it is not a major problem. The city feels safe even at night in most neighborhoods. There are no dangerous no-go areas. Zagreb has a laid-back, safe feeling. The 2020 earthquake caused some damage to buildings in the city center but the city has largely recovered. Natural hazards include occasional earthquakes (the area is seismically active). Overall, most expats feel very safe in Zagreb and crime is not a major concern in daily life. Traffic safety and the occasional earthquake are bigger concerns than crime.',
