      traffic: 'Moderate — traffic is manageable but getting worse as the city grows. Parking in the center is expensive. Trams usually faster than cars during rush hour.',
      best: 'Walking (for central locations). Trams (most routes). Living close to work. Biking is growing in popularity. Car useful for trips out of the city.',
      note: 'Commuting in Zagreb is relatively easy compared to larger European cities. The city is compact and the tram network covers most areas. Trams are frequent and reliable — they are the fastest way to get around during rush hour since they have dedicated tracks. Buses serve areas not covered by trams. Traffic is moderate but can be bad at peak times on main roads. Parking in the city center is expensive and hard to find. Many people bike — bike lanes are expanding. Zagreb Airport is about 20–30 minutes from the city center depending on traffic. For coastal trips, driving to the coast takes about 2–3 hours to Split or the Dalmatian coast (longer depending on traffic in summer). Overall, commuting in Zagreb is manageable and most people use trams or walk.',
