    taxes: {
      overview: 'Progressive income tax system with rates from 20% to 45%. VAT 25%. Social security contributions add significantly to the tax burden. Moderate to high tax rates but lower than Western Europe. The digital nomad visa has special tax treatment (30% flat).',
      income: 'Progressive personal income tax: 20% on income up to ~€42,000, 30% on income above. Surtaxes apply in some municipalities (up to 30% of tax = effectively up to 45% top rate for Zagreb). Moderate to high.',
      capitalGains: 'Capital gains tax: generally 20% for individuals. Some exemptions for primary residence. Moderate compared to many countries.',
      property: 'Property tax: very low — typically less than 0.2% of assessed value annually. One of the lowest in Europe. Local authorities set the rate.',
      sales: 'VAT (PDV): 25% standard rate. Reduced rates of 13% and 5% for certain goods (food, books, medicine). High VAT rate — among the highest in Europe.',
      corporate: 'Corporate income tax: 18% standard rate. Reduced rate of 10% for small businesses (revenue under ~€1 million). Competitive compared to many EU countries.',
      socialSecurity: 'Social security: employee ~20% (pension 15%, health 5%, etc.), employer ~16.5%. Total contributions are significant. Mandatory for employees.',
      note: 'Croatia has moderate to moderately high taxes. The top effective income tax rate (including surtax in Zagreb) can reach about 45% — lower than many Western European countries but higher than some Eastern European countries. VAT at 25% is among the highest in Europe. Social security contributions are also significant. However, the cost of living is much lower than Western Europe, so the overall standard of living can still be good. For digital nomads on the digital nomad visa, there is a special flat tax rate of 30% (with some deductions), which can be beneficial. For US citizens, you still need to file US tax returns — the Foreign Earned Income Exclusion and Foreign Tax Credit help reduce or eliminate double taxation. Croatia and the US have a tax treaty. Tax compliance can be complex — use a local tax advisor familiar with expat situations.',
    },
