      note: 'Split is generally a very safe city — one of the safer Mediterranean coastal tourist destinations. Violent crime is extremely rare. Petty theft (pickpocketing, bag/phone snatching) is the main concern, especially in crowded tourist areas like Diocletian Palace, the Riva waterfront, and on ferries — keep your belongings secure and be aware of your surroundings. Some tourist scams exist (restaurant overcharging, taxi scams) but they are less common than in many other European tourist cities. During peak summer season (July–August), the city is very crowded with tourists and petty crime increases. Traffic safety and being careful on the coastal roads are also considerations. Natural hazards include occasional wildfires in summer due to the dry Mediterranean climate. Overall, most expats feel very safe in Split and crime is not a major concern in daily life — the main safety issues are typical of any tourist destination.',
