      local: 'Austrian public schools are excellent and free. German medium. Very high quality education. Many expat children attend Austrian public schools, especially if they learn German. Highly regarded.',
      tuitionRange: '€7,000 – 28,000+ / year (international schools)',
      note: 'Vienna has excellent international schools. The American International School Vienna (AISV) is the main American/IB option and one of the top international schools in Europe. Vienna International School (VIS), the British School, Lycée Français, and many others serve the large expat community. Tuition is moderate to high by international standards. Many expat families live in Währing, Hietzing (13th district, near Schönbrunn), or other outer districts for proximity to top international schools. The Austrian public school system is also excellent and free — many expat children who speak German attend public schools. Vienna has numerous universities including the University of Vienna (founded 1365 — one of the oldest in Europe), Medical University of Vienna, and Vienna University of Economics and Business. Many English-language graduate programs are available. Overall, Vienna has one of the best education systems in Europe.',
