      traffic: 'Moderate — traffic is manageable but getting worse. Most people use public transit, bike, or walk. Parking in the center is expensive and limited.',
      best: 'Public transit (U-Bahn, tram, S-Bahn — excellent). Biking (growing, good bike lanes). Walking (for central locations). Very high quality of life with short commute times.',
      note: 'Commuting in Vienna is a breeze compared to most major cities. The public transit system (U-Bahn, trams, buses, S-Bahn) is one of the best in the world — fast, clean, reliable, frequent, and affordable. A monthly pass costs only about €55 and covers everything. Most commutes are 20–35 minutes door-to-door. The U-Bahn runs until midnight (24h on weekends) and trams run late too. Biking is also growing in popularity with expanding bike lanes. Many people walk to work if they live centrally. Traffic is moderate — not terrible but not great. Parking in the center is expensive and hard to find. Vienna Airport is about 30 minutes from the city center by S-Bahn or the CAT (City Airport Train). Overall, short commute times and excellent transit are major contributors to Vienna consistently ranking as one of the most livable cities in the world.',
