      note: 'Austria has a modern and well-developed banking system. Erste Bank / Sparkasse and Raiffeisen are the two largest bank groups and are everywhere. Bank Austria (part of UniCredit) is also major. Digital and online banking are good and improving. English service is available at major banks, especially in Vienna. Opening a bank account is relatively straightforward with a residence permit and proof of address (Meldebestätigung — you have to register your address within 3 days of moving in). N26 (German neobank) and Revolut are also very popular with expats for their ease of use, English interface, and low fees. Cash is still more commonly used in Austria than in some other European countries — many smaller shops and cafes prefer cash. However, cards and contactless payments are widely accepted at larger stores, restaurants, and supermarkets. Overall, banking in Austria is modern, reliable, and relatively easy for expats.',
