      note: 'Abu Dhabi is consistently ranked one of the safest cities in the world — and for good reason. Crime rates are extremely low, violent crime is almost non-existent, and even petty theft is very rare. The strict legal system, heavy policing, and harsh punishments are strong deterrents. You can leave your belongings unattended, walk alone at night, and generally feel very safe. The city is well-lit, clean, and orderly. The main safety considerations are traffic (aggressive driving can be an issue), summer heat (can be dangerous if you are not acclimated), and cultural sensitivities (you must respect local laws and customs, especially around public behavior, dress codes, and alcohol — which is only allowed in licensed venues). Overall, safety is one of the biggest advantages of living in Abu Dhabi — most expats feel extremely safe here.',
