      local: 'Public schools are for Emirati students only (Arabic medium). Expats must choose private/international schools. Many excellent options. Education is a big expense for expat families.',
      tuitionRange: 'AED 10,000 – 80,000+ / year (varies widely by school and grade)',
      note: 'Abu Dhabi has excellent international schools — some of the best in the Middle East. The American Community School (ACS) and American International School are the main American/IB options. British, French, German, Indian, and many other international schools are also available. Tuition is expensive — ranging from moderate to very high. However, many professional expat packages include education allowance for children. NYU Abu Dhabi is a top-tier university that is part of NYU. Many expat families live on Saadiyat Island or in areas near their children schools. The quality of international schools is generally very high with well-qualified teachers from around the world. Overall, excellent education options but tuition is a major expense.',
