      retirement: {
        duration: 'No dedicated retirement visa',
        income: 'N/A',
        desc: 'Vietnam does not have a dedicated retirement visa. Some retirees use long-term tourist visas or business visas. Not a common retirement destination officially despite the low cost of living. Visa runs are necessary for long-term stays.',
      },
      note: 'Vietnam has various visa options but the immigration system can be bureaucratic and confusing. Tourist e-visas (90 days) are easy to get online. For longer stays, work permits + temporary residence cards are the standard path for employed foreigners but require employer sponsorship and can be bureaucratic. There is no dedicated digital nomad visa yet — many digital nomads use tourist visas and do visa runs to nearby countries (Cambodia, Thailand, Malaysia) or get extensions. Investor visas are another option but require significant investment. Permanent residency is very difficult to obtain. Citizenship is extremely rare. Many expats use visa agents to help navigate the process. Vietnam has been discussing a digital nomad visa for years but nothing concrete as of 2024. Overall, short-term stays are easy but long-term residency requires work or investment and can be bureaucratic.',
