      scams: null,
      note: 'Panama City has moderate safety levels. Violent crime exists but is mostly concentrated in certain neighborhoods that expats generally avoid. Most expats live in areas like Punta Pacifica, El Cangrejo, San Francisco, and Obarrio — these are relatively safe. Petty theft (pickpocketing, phone theft, bag snatching) is more common, especially in crowded areas, on public transit, and in tourist spots like Casco Viejo. Be careful with your belongings and avoid displaying expensive items. Home burglaries can happen — many buildings have security. Scams exist, especially with taxi drivers refusing to use the meter and overcharging — always use Uber or insist on the meter. ATM skimming is a concern at standalone ATMs — use ATMs inside banks or malls. Traffic safety is another concern — drivers can be aggressive. Avoid walking in certain neighborhoods after dark (El Chorrillo, parts of San Miguelito). Overall, most expats feel safe in Panama City if they use normal precautions and live in the right neighborhoods.',
