      retirement: {
        duration: 'Pensionado Visa — permanent residency (retirement)',
        income: '$1,000+ USD monthly pension income (or $750 + $100 per dependent)',
        desc: 'The Panama Pensionado Visa is one of the most popular retirement visas in the world. Requires a lifetime pension income of $1,000+/month. Benefits include discounts on flights, restaurants, hotels, medical services, and more. Permanent residency. Very popular with American retirees.',
      },
      note: 'Panama has one of the most accessible and attractive immigration systems for Americans and other nationalities. The Pensionado Visa (retirement visa) is world-famous for its generous benefits and low income requirement ($1,000/month pension). The Friendly Nations Visa is another popular path — it offers permanent residency for citizens of 50+ friendly countries (including the US) through real estate investment ($200k+), bank deposit ($200k+), or business investment. The Digital Nomad Visa was introduced more recently for remote workers. Panama also offers investor visas and work visas. Citizenship is possible after 5 years of permanent residency — one of the shorter paths in Latin America. The use of the US dollar makes financial integration easy for Americans. Overall, Panama has some of the most accessible residency and citizenship paths in the Americas — a major reason it has such a large expat community.',
