      note: 'Kandy has fewer international school options than Colombo. Kandy International School is the main international option. There are also well-regarded local private schools like Trinity College (boys) and Hillwood College (girls) — these follow the Sri Lankan curriculum but are considered prestigious and affordable. Tuition is much cheaper than international schools in Colombo. Many expat families in Kandy either homeschool their children or send them to local private schools for cultural immersion. The University of Peradeniya is one of the top universities in Sri Lanka and is located just outside Kandy. For families wanting a full international curriculum, Colombo has more options and is about 2.5–3 hours away. Overall, education options are more limited and more local in Kandy compared to the capital, which is one reason fewer expat families choose to live here long-term.',
