      priceLevel: 'Very affordable — €120–180/month for single person cooking at home. Restaurant meals: €5–10 at tapas bars, €8–15 at nicer places. Granada is famous for free tapas — many bars give a free tapa with every drink.',
      organicNote: 'Granada is a foodie paradise — famous for its free tapas culture (order a drink and you get a free plate of food). The city is known for Andalusian specialties like gazpacho, jamón ibérico, and pescaíto frito. Arab-influenced food is also big — pastries, baklava, and tea houses (teterías) in the Albaicín. The Alpujarras mountains nearby produce amazing ham (Jamón de Trevélez) and cheese. Fresh mountain produce is excellent. Granada-style tapas are legendary — you can eat very well for very little money. Wine from nearby Andalusia is cheap and good. Imported goods are more limited than in bigger cities but available.',
