    mapLocation: 'In northern Spain, on the Bay of Biscay, in the Basque Country. The city sits in a valley along the Nervión river, surrounded by green hills. Casco Viejo (Old Town) is the historic seven streets — pintxos bars, the cathedral, and the oldest part of the city. Abando is the modern city center — the Guggenheim, Gran Vía (main shopping street), and the main train station. Indautxu is a central residential neighborhood — tree-lined streets, shops, and a more upscale feel. Deusto is the university and residential district on the other side of the river — the University of Deusto, parks, and a quiet atmosphere. Bilbao is famous for its Guggenheim Museum (Frank Gehry\'s iconic titanium building), the ría (estuary), its industrial past turned modern cultural hub, Basque culture and language (Euskera), and exceptional food (pintxos — Basque tapas). The metro is one of the most modern in Europe (designed by Norman Foster).',
