      organicNote: 'Bilbao and the Basque Country have some of the best food in the world. Pintxos (Basque tapas) are the star — tiny pieces of art on bread, washed down with Basque cider or txakoli wine. The region has the highest concentration of Michelin stars per capita in the world. Fresh seafood from the Bay of Biscay is excellent. Idiazabal cheese (Basque sheep cheese), txakoli wine, and sidra (cider) are all local specialties. Mercado de la Ribera is a historic food hall. El Corte Inglés has imported goods. The Basque Country is more expensive than other parts of Spain but the food quality is exceptional. The local cuisine is heavily seafood and meat-based with French influence.',
