    mapLocation: 'On the Bay of Biscay in the Basque Country, near the French border. The city is famous for the spectacular La Concha beach — a crescent of golden sand framed by Monte Urgull and Monte Igueldo. Parte Vieja (Old Town) is the historic center with hundreds of pintxo bars and narrow cobblestone streets. Gros is the residential neighborhood east of the center — Zurriola beach, surf culture, cafes, and a younger vibe. Centro is the elegant city center with the main shopping street and Belle Époque architecture. Antiguo is the upscale neighborhood west of the center — residential, quiet, and closer to the beach. San Sebastián (Donostia in Basque) is known for having the highest density of Michelin stars per capita in the world, its pintxos culture, La Concha (often ranked one of the best urban beaches in Europe), the San Sebastián International Film Festival, and Basque culture.',
