      organicNote: 'San Sebastián is one of the great food cities of the world. It has the highest concentration of Michelin stars per capita on Earth (more than Tokyo, Paris, or New York). Pintxos (Basque tapas) are an art form here — try the Parte Vieja old town pintxo bars and do a "pintxo crawl" (txikiteo). Local specialties include bacalao al pil-pil (cod), txangurro (spider crab), Idiazabal cheese, and fresh seafood from the Bay of Biscay. Txakoli (dry white wine) and sidra (Basque cider) are the iconic drinks. The Basque Country produces exceptional seafood, cheese, and meat. The food scene is simply world-class — from humble pintxo bars to 3-Michelin-star temples of gastronomy. Imported goods are available but the local food is so good you won\'t miss them.',
