      priceLevel: 'Moderate — €200–300/month for single person cooking at home. Restaurant meals: €8–15 at tapas bars, €15–25 at nicer places. Fresh seafood is excellent. Tourist areas are more expensive but local areas are very affordable.',
      organicNote: 'Mallorca has excellent food — fresh seafood from the Mediterranean, sobrassada (local cured sausage), ensaïmada (sweet pastry), and plenty of local produce. The Serra de Tramuntana region produces olive oil, almonds, and citrus fruits. The island has a big food scene with many good restaurants — from local tapas bars to Michelin-starred dining. British and German imports are widely available due to the large expat populations — you can find Marmite, baked beans, German bread, etc. Mercat de l\'Olivar is a great central food market. Local wine from the Binissalem region is surprisingly good. Food prices are higher than mainland Spain but still very reasonable compared to Northern Europe or the US.',
