    mapLocation: 'On the Island of Montreal in Quebec, Canada. Plateau Mont-Royal is the iconic bohemian neighborhood — colorful row houses with exterior staircases, indie shops, cafes, and the "cool" heart of Montreal. Mile End is the trendy creative neighborhood north of the Plateau — bagels, indie music, artists, and a laid-back vibe. Old Montreal (Vieux-Montréal) is the historic district — cobblestone streets, the Old Port, Notre-Dame Basilica, and European charm. Griffintown is the formerly industrial neighborhood turned trendy — condos, restaurants, breweries, and young professionals. Montreal is a bilingual (French and English) city with a unique European-North American hybrid culture. It is famous for its food scene (bagels, smoked meat, poutine), festivals (Just for Laughs, Jazz Festival), and affordable cost of living compared to Toronto or Vancouver.',
