      organicNote: 'Montreal has an incredible food scene — often called the food capital of Canada. The city is famous for bagels (St-Viateur and Fairmount are the two legendary bagel shops), smoked meat (Schwartz\'s), poutine, and its diverse cuisine reflecting the city\'s immigrant communities. Jean-Talon Market is a food lover\'s paradise — fresh produce, cheese, charcuterie, bread, flowers, and more. The city has one of the highest concentrations of restaurants per capita in North America. French and European specialty foods are widely available. Organic and health food stores like Rachelle-Béry and Avril are popular. The Plateau and Mile End are packed with excellent cafes, bakeries, and restaurants at every price point.',
