      organicNote: 'Kelowna and the Okanagan Valley have an incredible food scene centered around local produce — stone fruits (peaches, cherries, apricots), apples, grapes, and vegetables from the fertile valley. The region is famous for its wineries — over 200 in the Okanagan Valley, producing world-class reds and whites (Pinot Noir, Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon, Riesling, and more). Farm-to-table restaurants are abundant. The Kelowna Farmers Market is one of the best in BC. Cideries, craft breweries, and distilleries are also thriving. Local fruit (especially Okanagan peaches and cherries) is legendary — cheap and amazing when in season. The region has a strong local food culture.',
