            desc: 'David is the second-largest city in Panama and the commercial and agricultural hub of the Chiriquí region. The city serves as a gateway to Boquete (45min), Bocas del Toro (3hr), and the Costa Rican border (1.5hr). Downtown David is a bustling commercial center with markets, malls (Mall Chiriquí, the largest outside Panama City), banks, restaurants, and government offices. The city has a warm, tropical climate and a relaxed pace compared to Panama City. It offers all the amenities of a medium-sized city at a lower cost.',
