            desc: 'Galle Fort is a UNESCO World Heritage site and one of the best-preserved colonial fortifications in Asia. Built by the Portuguese in the 16th century and extensively developed by the Dutch in the 17th century, the fort is a walled city within a city — full of Dutch colonial villas, boutique hotels, art galleries, cafes, and restaurants. The ramparts offer stunning ocean views and are popular for sunset walks. The fort has a unique atmosphere — a mix of colonial history, Sri Lankan culture, and expat-owned businesses. It\'s one of Sri Lanka\'s most atmospheric and beautiful places to live.',
