            title: 'Slow-Paced Coastal Living',
            desc: 'Galle offers a slow, relaxed pace of life on Sri Lanka\'s south coast. The city is small enough to walk everywhere. Beaches are nearby — Unawatuna (15min), Hikkaduwa (20min), and Mirissa (45min) — famous for swimming, surfing, and whale watching. A single expat can live very comfortably on $700–1,100/month including rent. Sri Lankan food is delicious and cheap — rice and curry, fresh seafood, tropical fruit, and hoppers are everyday meals. The main downsides: hot and humid climate, limited job opportunities, and Sri Lanka\'s economic situation (inflation, currency instability).',
