        description: 'Express Entry is Canada\'s flagship economic immigration system. It is not a visa itself — it is a system that manages applications for three economic immigration programs: Federal Skilled Worker (FSW), Federal Skilled Trades (FST), and Canadian Experience Class (CEC). Candidates create an online profile and are scored on the Comprehensive Ranking System (CRS) based on age, education, language skills (English/French), work experience, and other factors. IRCC holds regular draws and invites the highest-scoring candidates to apply for permanent residency. A provincial nomination (PNP) adds 600 CRS points — practically guaranteeing an invitation. Express Entry is known for being relatively fast compared to other PR pathways — targeted processing time of 6 months for 80% of complete applications, though actual times have varied.',
        eligible: 'Skilled workers with 1+ year of continuous full-time (or equivalent) skilled work experience; must meet minimum language requirements (CLB 7 for FSW)',
