        description: 'US citizens are eligible for visa-free entry to Thailand for tourism purposes. If arriving by air, you typically get 30 days stamped in your passport at the airport. If arriving by land, you also get 30 days (limited to 2 land border entries per calendar year from neighboring countries, with some variations). A single-entry tourist visa (obtained in advance from a Thai embassy/consulate) gives you 60 days on arrival, which can then be extended by 30 days at a Thai immigration office for a fee of ฿1,900. You cannot work on a tourist visa or visa-exempt entry. Multiple "visa runs" (leaving and re-entering to reset the tourist clock) used to be common but have become more heavily scrutinized in recent years.',
        eligible: 'US citizens and citizens of 60+ visa-exempt countries',
