        description: 'Greece\'s Golden Visa program grants 5-year renewable residency to non-EU citizens who invest in Greece. The most popular route is real estate investment. Following changes in 2024, the minimum investment was raised to €400,000 for properties in Athens and other prime areas (up from €250,000), and €800,000 for certain zones. There is also a €250,000 option for renovations of non-residential/agricultural properties in specific areas. The visa is renewable every 5 years as long as the investment is maintained. After 5–7 years, you can apply for permanent residency and potentially Greek citizenship. The program is very popular with Americans, Chinese, and other non-EU investors.',
