        keyRequirements: 'Minimum monthly income of approximately €3,500 (for single applicant; higher for family). Employment/contract with foreign company or self-employment/freelance income from abroad. Health insurance coverage valid in Greece. Clean criminal record. Proof of accommodation in Greece.',
        usFriendly: 90,
        placeholder: false,
        description: 'Greece introduced a digital nomad visa specifically for remote workers who want to live in Greece while working for employers or clients outside of Greece. The visa is valid for 1 year initially and can be renewed for longer periods. It allows you to live in Greece and work remotely for foreign companies or as a freelancer serving foreign clients. The income requirement is approximately €3,500 per month for a single applicant (add 50% for a spouse and 25% per child). Greece is increasingly popular with digital nomads due to its beautiful climate, low cost of living (compared to Western Europe), rich history, and excellent food. Combined with the Non-Dom tax regime (which can exempt foreign income from Greek tax for 7 years), it is a very competitive option for American remote workers.',
