        usFriendly: 88,
        placeholder: false,
        description: 'The Financially Independent Person (FIP) visa — also called the "retirement visa" or "passive income visa" — is for people who have sufficient stable income from foreign sources to support themselves in Greece without working. This is a popular option for American retirees, early retirees, and people living off investments or rental income. The visa is initially issued for 2 years and is renewable as long as you continue to meet the income requirement. You cannot work in Greece on this visa — all income must come from abroad. Combined with Greece\'s Non-Dom tax regime (which can exempt your foreign income from Greek tax for 7 years), the FIP visa is very attractive for retirees and financially independent expats. Greece\'s warm climate, low cost of living, and beautiful islands make it a popular retirement destination for Americans.',
        eligible: 'Non-EU/EEA citizens with sufficient, regular, passive or non-Greek income. US citizens are eligible. Must not work or engage in business activities in Greece.',
