        usFriendly: 60,
        placeholder: false,
        description: 'If you have a job offer from a Greek employer, you can apply for a Greek work permit and employment visa. The process is employer-driven — your employer must first apply for a work permit from the Greek authorities and demonstrate that no EU/EEA citizen is available to fill the position (this is called the labor market test). Once the work permit is approved, you then apply for the entry visa at a Greek consulate. Work permits are tied to a specific employer and job — you cannot switch jobs without a new permit. Jobs in fields like teaching (especially English at international schools), tourism, shipping, IT, and academia are more accessible for foreigners. Finding a Greek employer willing and able to sponsor a work permit is the main challenge for most Americans.',
