        usFriendly: 85,
        placeholder: false,
        description: 'If you want to study in Greece at a university, language school, or other recognized educational program, you will need a Greek student visa (Type D visa for long-term study). Greece has many excellent universities, including the University of Athens, Aristotle University of Thessaloniki, and the American College of Greece (Deree). There are also many Greek language programs and study-abroad opportunities. The student visa allows you to stay in Greece for the duration of your program and work part-time (limited hours). For degree programs, the tuition at public Greek universities is very low compared to US schools (especially for EU students; international tuition may be higher). American students often study abroad in Greece for a semester or a year, while some pursue full degree programs. Student life in Greece is vibrant, affordable, and culturally rich.',
