        usFriendly: 75,
        placeholder: false,
        description: 'If you have a family member who is a Greek citizen or legal resident of Greece, you may be able to join them through family reunification. This applies to spouses, minor children, and in some cases dependent parents or other close family members. The sponsor (the family member already in Greece) must demonstrate they have sufficient income to support the joining family member(s) and adequate housing. Family reunification is a well-established path and is generally straightforward if you meet the relationship and financial requirements. For American citizens married to Greek citizens or Greek residents, this is one of the most common routes to moving to Greece. The process involves proving the family relationship, meeting financial and housing criteria, and applying for the appropriate visa and residence permit.',
