    safetyScore: 45,
    safetySummary: 'Metro Manila has moderate-to-high crime. Expat areas like BGC, Makati, and Alabang are generally safe with 24/7 security. Petty crime and occasional violent crime happen in poorer areas. Exercise strong precautions outside expat zones.',
    safetyViolent: 'Medium — violent crime exists, especially in slum areas and poorer neighborhoods. Expats in upscale areas are rarely affected but should be cautious.',
    safetyPetty: 'High — pickpocketing, bag snatching, phone theft, and taxi/Grab scams are common, especially in crowded areas, public transit, and tourist districts.',
    safetyNight: 'Medium-low — avoid walking alone at night outside expat areas. Use Grab. BGC and Makati are relatively safe at night within their boundaries.',
    safetyScams: 'High — be very cautious with "friendly" strangers, taxi scams, fake officials, credit card fraud, and online scams. Only use licensed transportation.',
    safetyNote: 'Manila safety picture is very mixed. Upscale, gated communities and business districts (BGC, Makati, Alabang) are generally safe and have private security. But the surrounding areas can be dangerous. Common sense precautions: use Grab, do not walk alone at night, keep valuables hidden, be careful with your phone, and be wary of scams. Terrorism is a concern in the southern Philippines but rare in Manila.',
    hcRating: '6.5 / 10',
