    expatEnglish: 'Very High — English is an official language. Everyone from taxi drivers to CEOs speaks English. The Philippines is the third-largest English-speaking country in the world. You never need to learn Tagalog to live here, though it is helpful and appreciated.',
    schoolsSummary: 'Manila has excellent international schools with high standards. The International School Manila is one of the best in Asia. Tuition is expensive but cheaper than Singapore or Hong Kong.',
