    safetySummary: 'Cebu is generally moderate in safety. Tourist areas and expat neighborhoods are relatively safe. Petty crime is common and some areas can be dangerous at night. Exercise normal to high precautions.',
    safetyViolent: 'Medium — violent crime exists but expats in good neighborhoods are rarely targeted. Most violence is related to drugs and poverty in certain areas.',
    safetyPetty: 'High — pickpocketing, phone theft, and bag snatching are common in crowded areas, on public transit, and in tourist spots. Thieves on motorcycles are a known issue.',
    safetyNight: 'Medium-low — avoid walking alone at night outside tourist/expat areas. Use Grab. IT Park and Ayala are relatively safe at night.',
    safetyScams: 'Medium — be cautious with taxi scams, fake tour operators, gem scams, and overly friendly strangers. Always negotiate fares in advance or use Grab.',
    safetyNote: 'Cebu is less safe than Manila upscale areas but comparable to other mid-sized Philippine cities. The main issues are petty theft, occasional taxi scams, and motorbike-related crime. Use Grab, be careful with your belongings, avoid dark areas at night, and use common sense. Typhoon safety is also a concern — the Philippines gets typhoons.',
    hcRating: '6 / 10',
