    climateBest: 'June–September (dry season — less rain, more sun)',
    climateWorst: 'January–February (wettest months with risk of flooding in low-lying areas)',
    climateRain: 'About 1,800mm annually. Heavy rain during wet season. Flooding is a recurring problem in many parts of Jakarta during the rainy season.',
    expatSize: 'Large expat community — estimated 100,000+ foreigners in Jakarta. Includes corporate expats, diplomats, teachers, digital nomads, and entrepreneurs.',
    expatUS: 'Smaller American community — embassy staff, corporate expats, teachers, and some entrepreneurs. Less than in Philippines or Thailand.',
    expatGroups: ['InterNations Jakarta', 'American Club Jakarta', 'American Women Association', 'Jakarta Expats (largest Facebook group)', 'Jakarta Digital Nomads'],
    expatHangouts: ['SCBD (rooftop bars and fine dining)', 'Kemang (restaurants, bars, expat hub)', 'Menteng (cafes and colonial charm)', 'Senayan/Sudirman (malls and business)', 'Ancol (beach and entertainment)'],
    expatEnglish: 'Medium — better among younger people, professionals, and in expat areas. Business English is common in multinational companies. In daily life outside expat zones, Indonesian is needed. Learning basic Bahasa Indonesia is highly recommended.',
