    bankFees: 'Low to moderate fees. ATM fees: Rp 5,000–10,000 ($0.30–0.65) at other bank ATMs. International transfer fees vary.',
    bankATMs: 'ATMs are everywhere in cities. Most accept Visa/Mastercard but some only work with local cards. Withdrawal limits vary.',
    bankCards: 'Debit and credit cards widely accepted in malls, restaurants, and larger shops. Cash is still very common for small transactions, markets, and local food.',
    bankOnline: 'BCA has the best mobile app and internet banking — widely considered the best in Indonesia. Mandiri and other banks have improving digital services. Mobile wallets like GoPay, OVO, and DANA are extremely popular.',
    bankNote: 'BCA is the clear favorite among expats for its excellent mobile app and widespread ATMs. Citibank offers premium services but is less common. Mobile wallets (GoPay, OVO, DANA) are used for everything from food delivery to taxi to paying at street vendors. Opening an account typically requires a KITAS residence permit, which can be a barrier for tourists and short-term visitors.',
