    expatEnglish: 'Medium — better among younger people, professionals, and those working in tourism/hospitality. Most doctors speak English. In daily life, Spanish is essential — you will need it for shopping, transit, and dealing with bureaucracy. Many expats take Spanish classes upon arrival.',
    schoolsSummary: 'Quito has several good international schools. Alliance Academy International is the most popular with American expats. Tuition is moderate compared to other international cities.',
