    schoolsLocal: 'Ecuadorian public schools are free and accessible. Quality varies. Instruction is in Spanish. Many expat families choose private bilingual schools for better quality and cultural immersion.',
    schoolsTuitionRange: '$8,000 – 22,000+ / year',
    schoolsNote: 'Alliance Academy and Colegio Americano are the top American/international schools. The British School and German School are also popular options. Tuition is significantly lower than in the US or other international cities. Many international schools are located in or near Cumbayá, which is why many expat families choose to live there.',
    commuteDesc: 'Traffic has improved since the new metro opened. Commutes within the city are manageable. The long north-south layout of the city means traveling from one end to the other can take time.',
    commuteAvg: '20–45 minutes depending on distance. The metro has significantly reduced commute times.',
