    commuteTraffic: 'Moderate to heavy at rush hour. The new metro has helped. Main roads (Av. Amazonas, Av. 6 de Diciembre, Av. Eloy Alfaro) get congested. Hilly terrain can make some routes slow.',
    commuteBest: 'Live near your workplace or near a metro station. La Floresta, La Mariscal, and La Carolina are centrally located. Cumbayá is popular with families but requires a commute to the city center (about 20–30 min by car).',
    commuteNote: 'The Quito Metro (opened 2023) has been a game-changer for public transit — it is fast, modern, and cheap. Taxis are very affordable. Uber and Cabify are popular for safety and comfort. Many expats who live in Cumbayá drive or use private transport to get to the city. The city long north-south layout means commute times vary significantly depending on direction.',
    netSpeed: 'Good — 30–100Mbps widely available. Speeds and reliability are decent. Fiber is available in most nice neighborhoods. Adequate for remote work.',
