    schoolsLocal: 'Croatian public schools are free and available. Instruction in Croatian. Good quality but language barrier for most expat families.',
    schoolsTuitionRange: '€8,000 – 18,000 / year',
    schoolsNote: 'International school options are more limited than in Zagreb, which is why Split is more popular with singles, couples, retirees, and child-free digital nomads than with families. Some expat families homeschool or use online schools. The University of Split is growing and offers some programs in English. Overall, Split is more of a lifestyle destination than a family expat hub.',
    commuteDesc: 'Short commutes — Split is a compact city. Most places are walkable or a short bus ride. Traffic can be bad in summer tourist season.',
    commuteAvg: '10–25 minutes for most commutes within the city',
