    commuteBest: 'Living near the center means you can walk almost everywhere. Buses connect outer neighborhoods to the center. Many people bike.',
    commuteNote: 'Split is small enough that most commutes are short. Walking is the best way to get around the center. Buses cover the wider city. In summer, traffic gets worse due to tourism — but most expats who live in the center walk or bike everywhere. Ferry connections to the islands make Split a great base for island hopping. Many people work remotely and enjoy the lifestyle rather than commuting to traditional jobs.',
