    bankOverview: 'Modern, well-developed banking system dominated by Sparkasse (savings banks) and Raiffeisen (cooperative banks). Neobanks like N26 and Revolut are very popular with expats. SEPA transfers are free within the EU.',
    bankReq: 'Meldebestätigung (registration certificate from the municipality), passport, proof of employment/income, residence permit. N26 and Revolut can be opened with just a passport (no Meldebestätigung needed initially).',
    bankFees: 'Low to moderate. Many accounts have monthly fees of €3–8. ATMs at your bank are free. Other ATMs may charge fees. SEPA transfers are free.',
    bankATMs: 'ATMs (Bankomaten) are everywhere. Most accept Visa/Mastercard. Cash is still commonly used in Austria — many small shops and cafes prefer cash or do not accept cards at all (especially in traditional establishments).',
    bankCards: 'Debit and credit cards are widely accepted in larger stores, restaurants, and hotels. However, Austria is more cash-based than many other Western European countries — you will need cash regularly. Maestro debit cards are common. Apple Pay / Google Pay growing but not universal.',
    bankOnline: 'Good online and mobile banking. Erste Bank (George app) and Raiffeisen have decent apps. N26 has the best mobile experience. Online banking is standard but in-person banking is still common in Austria.',
    bankNote: 'Opening a traditional bank account in Austria requires a Meldebestätigung (registration certificate) which you get after registering your address at the Magistrat (city hall). This can take a few weeks. N26 and Revolut are popular options for new arrivals because you can open an account with just a passport. Austria is relatively cash-heavy compared to Netherlands or Scandinavian countries — always carry some cash. Many traditional shops, cafes, and even restaurants only accept cash or debit cards (not credit cards). Maestro is the common debit card system. Direct debit (Lastschrift) is standard for recurring bills.',
    scores: { costIndex: 32, safety: 85, healthcare: 90, education: 90, internet: 88, walkability: 88, expatCommunity: 80, climate: 70 },
