    accountType: 'Savings account with Pao Tang digital services',
    accountOverview:
      'Krungthai Bank is a state-owned Thai bank and one of the largest banks in the country by branch network. Because it is government-owned, it has branches everywhere — even in small towns and rural areas where other banks have no presence. For expats living outside of major cities, Krungthai is often the most accessible bank. The bank is known for low fees and reliable basic banking services. Krungthai\'s digital banking includes the Pao Tang app and government-linked services (since the bank handles many government payment programs). However, English language service quality varies significantly between branches — major Bangkok branches may have English-speaking staff, but smaller provincial branches probably do not. For expats, Krungthai can be a good secondary bank or a good choice if you live outside Bangkok, but it is generally not the first choice for primary banking due to variable foreigner service and a less polished app.',
