    accountOverview:
      'Banco Nacional de Costa Rica (BNCR) is the largest bank in Costa Rica by total assets and branch network. It is 100% state-owned, which means all deposits are backed by the Costa Rican government — making it one of the safest banks in the country. Banco Nacional has branches and ATMs in every corner of the country, including small towns and rural areas where private banks have no presence. For expats, Banco Nacional is a good choice for basic banking and for accessing services outside of San José. The bank offers savings accounts, checking accounts, fixed deposits, loans, and more. English service quality varies significantly — major branches in San José and Escazú have English-speaking staff, but branches in smaller towns usually do not. The bank\'s digital banking platform (Banco en Línea) is functional but less polished than private banks like BAC.',
