    accountOverview:
      'N26 is a German neobank (mobile-first bank) that has become very popular across Europe, including with expats in Greece. Founded in Berlin in 2013, N26 offers a fully digital banking experience with a euro current account, debit card, and mobile app. N26 is a fully licensed German bank, which means your deposits are protected by the German deposit guarantee scheme up to €100,000 — the same protection as any traditional bank. For expats in Greece, N26 is popular because you can open an account easily online (no branch visit), the app is clean and well-designed, and it works seamlessly across the EU with SEPA transfers and direct debits. Like Revolut, N26 is a great complement to a traditional Greek bank account but not a full replacement — you still need a local bank for some Greek-specific payments and administrative purposes.',
